    "narrative": "The core of today\u2019s offensive strategy for LawDog centers on **Bryson Stott** and **Daulton Varsho**, who represent our highest-ceiling plays. **Bryson Stott** (72.46) carries the day\u2019s strongest projection, heavily buoyed by an 18% boost from facing a vulnerable pitcher in V\u00e1squez. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** (65.35) is an elite start; he benefits from a positive platoon split against a right-handed pitcher and, crucially, receives a tactical bump for his stolen base potential against a slow-delivering pitcher, which aligns with our organizational priority of aggressively chasing the scarcest category. **Gleyber Torres** (60.60) also cracks the 60-point threshold, utilizing a prime leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Matz to solidify his place in the lineup.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the fringes of the roster, where **Masyn Winn** (39.49) fell just short of the 40-point \"Strong\" threshold. Despite a respectable base projection, the high xERA of Eovaldi suppressed **Masyn Winn**\u2019s ceiling, leading the optimizer to bench him in favor of protecting our daily game cap. We are also monitoring the availability of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while **Lawrence Butler** and **Will Smith** are held out of the starting lineup today. While **Jonathan Aranda** (57.71), **Taylor Ward** (57.10), and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (56.07) are relegated to the sub-60 range, they remain viable starts in standard formats, though we remain wary of the heavy SP-skill penalties facing **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Taylor Ward** against their respective left-handed opponents. **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman** round out the roster but face tough sledding against Harrison, functioning primarily as floor-fillers today.",
